# Build-context exclusions for the stark-translate Dockerfile.
#
# Keep this list aggressive — without it, `docker buildx build` would copy
# ~60 GB of training data, model weights, and cached venvs into the
# context tarball before COPY can pick the few directories we actually
# want. That blows up GHCR build times and hits the 10 GB context limit
# on hosted runners.
#
# Anything we genuinely need is named in the Dockerfile's COPY directives:
#   pyproject.toml README.md operator_app/ engines/ tools/ features/
#   displays/ scripts/ settings.py dry_run_ab.py models.lock.json
#   start_server.sh run_operator.sh docker/

# --- Training data + outputs (none of this belongs in the runtime image) ---
stt-data/
stark_data/
bible_data/
whisper_ablation/
hybrid_runs/
ablation/
metrics/

# --- Bundled model weights — bind-mounted at runtime, never baked ---
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.ckpt

# --- Python virtual envs + caches ---
.venv/
venv/
stt_env/
stt_train_env/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# --- Build artefacts ---
build/
dist/
*.whl
*.tar.gz

# --- Editor / OS ---
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- Git + CI ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Secrets / local config ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem
docker/.env

# --- Docs (not needed at runtime; readme is force-included via Dockerfile) ---
docs/
CLAUDE*.md
*.md
!README.md

# --- Other ---
node_modules/
*.log
*.csv
*.jsonl
!models.lock.json
